.el .ds Aq '
.TH timebook 1 2026-11-19 "sandogasa 0.28.2" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
timebook \- Find free Fedora meeting rooms and check bookings in Fedora Calendar
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtimebook\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fedora\*(Aqs shared meeting rooms (meeting, meeting\-1, ...) as Fedora Calendar books them: which rooms a planned meeting, or a series of them, would find free, and what each room holds.
.PP
A calendar entry\*(Aqs location is free text, so one room appears under many names (meeting\-1@chat.fedoraproject.org, a matrix.to link, the IRC channel it replaced); timebook reads them all as the room. Times are compared in UTC.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS timebook check
\fBtimebook check\fR [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-suggest\fR] [\fB\-\-tz\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIROOM\fR> <\fIAT\fR>
.PP
Check whether a room is free for a planned meeting or series
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 1]
How many meetings in the series (1 to 520)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<EVERY>\fR [default: 7]
Days between meetings (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-minutes\fR \fI<MINUTES>\fR [default: 60]
How long each meeting is, in minutes (1 to 1440)
.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR
Check whether the meetings in a taken room still take place
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\fR \fI<TZ>\fR [default: UTC]
The time zone of AT, e.g. Europe/Dublin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIROOM\fR>
The room: meeting, meeting\-1, or any name of it
.TP
<\fIAT\fR>
When the first one starts: YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM, in \-\-tz
.SS timebook find
\fBtimebook find\fR [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-suggest\fR] [\fB\-\-tz\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAT\fR>
.PP
Find the rooms free for a planned meeting or series
.PP
When no room is free for every meeting, or with \-\-suggest, the meetings in the taken rooms are looked up in meetbot: a room whose meetings have had no minutes in the last 12 weeks is shown as likely free, with the evidence.
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 1]
How many meetings in the series (1 to 520)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<EVERY>\fR [default: 7]
Days between meetings (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-minutes\fR \fI<MINUTES>\fR [default: 60]
How long each meeting is, in minutes (1 to 1440)
.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR
Check whether the meetings in a taken room still take place
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\fR \fI<TZ>\fR [default: UTC]
The time zone of AT, e.g. Europe/Dublin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIAT\fR>
When the first one starts: YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM, in \-\-tz
.SS timebook rooms
\fBtimebook rooms\fR [\fB\-\-days\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
List what each room holds in a period
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR [default: 28]
Days to cover (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
First day (YYYY\-MM\-DD; default today)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS timebook stale
\fBtimebook stale\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\fR] [\fB\-\-weeks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Check whether recurring meetings still take place
.PP
Each recurring entry of the last weeks is looked for in meetbot\*(Aqs minutes (by its calendar\*(Aqs name and its title as a topic), an occurrence counting as held when minutes in its room start within an hour of it. For a series without any, its owners\*(Aq last activity on Discourse is shown. Series that stopped at 2025\-12\-31, fedocal\*(Aqs old default end for a series without one, are listed with any minutes since: those may still be held.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
Ask meetbot again instead of using answers from the last day
.TP
\fB\-\-weeks\fR \fI<WEEKS>\fR [default: 12]
Weeks back to look (1 to 52)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
